.SH NAME
X509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags, X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags \- X509 hostname verification flags
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\& #include <openssl/x509_vfy.h>
\&
\& void X509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags(X509_VERIFY_PARAM *param,
\&                                      unsigned int flags);
\& unsigned int X509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags(const X509_VERIFY_PARAM *param);
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Host flags control how hostname matching is performed during certificate
verification: which wildcard forms are permitted in the certificate\*(Aqs subject
alternative name (SAN) entries, and whether the certificate\*(Aqs subject
distinguished name is consulted in addition to the SAN.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags()\fR sets the host flags on \fIparam\fR to
\&\fIflags\fR, for use during subsequent calls to \fBX509_verify_cert\fR\|(3).
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags()\fR returns any host flags previously set via a
call to \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags()\fR.
.PP
The \fIflags\fR default to 0. They may be set to a bitwise OR of the following:
.IP \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_ALWAYS_CHECK_SUBJECT\fR 4
.IX Item "X509_CHECK_FLAG_ALWAYS_CHECK_SUBJECT"
.PD 0
.IP \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT\fR 4
.IX Item "X509_CHECK_FLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT"
.IP \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_NO_WILDCARDS\fR 4
.IX Item "X509_CHECK_FLAG_NO_WILDCARDS"
.IP \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_NO_PARTIAL_WILDCARDS\fR 4
.IX Item "X509_CHECK_FLAG_NO_PARTIAL_WILDCARDS"
.IP \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_MULTI_LABEL_WILDCARDS\fR 4
.IX Item "X509_CHECK_FLAG_MULTI_LABEL_WILDCARDS"
.IP \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_SINGLE_LABEL_SUBDOMAINS\fR 4
.IX Item "X509_CHECK_FLAG_SINGLE_LABEL_SUBDOMAINS"
.PD
.PP
By default the subject distinguished name is not consulted; matching is
performed only against the subject alternative name extension.
.PP
The \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_ALWAYS_CHECK_SUBJECT\fR flag causes the function to
also match against the subject DN (the \fBcommonName\fR attribute for DNS
names, the \fBemailAddress\fR attribute for email addresses), whether or not
the certificate contains a subject alternative name of the corresponding
type.  During certificate chain verification this flag additionally
causes DNS name constraints to be applied to the subject \fBcommonName\fR
of the leaf certificate, since the \fBcommonName\fR may then be used as a
DNS identity; see \fBNAME_CONSTRAINTS_check\fR\|(3).
.PP
The \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT\fR flag suppresses matching against
the subject DN. As that is already the default, this flag has an effect
only in combination with \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_ALWAYS_CHECK_SUBJECT\fR, over
which it takes precedence.
.PP
If set, \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_NO_WILDCARDS\fR disables wildcard
expansion.
.PP
If set, \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_NO_PARTIAL_WILDCARDS\fR suppresses support
for "*" as wildcard pattern in labels that have a prefix or suffix,
such as: "www*" or "*www".
.PP
If set, \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_MULTI_LABEL_WILDCARDS\fR allows a "*" that
constitutes the complete label of a DNS name (e.g. "*.example.com")
to match more than one label in the configured reference identifier.
.PP
If set, \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_SINGLE_LABEL_SUBDOMAINS\fR restricts reference
identifiers which start with ".", that would otherwise match any
sub\-domain in the peer certificate, to only match direct child
sub\-domains. Thus, for instance, with this flag set a reference
identifier of ".example.com" would match a peer certificate with a DNS
name of "www.example.com", but would not match a peer certificate with
a DNS name of "www.sub.example.com".
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUES"
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_hostflags()\fR returns the flag values.
